{{!-- TYPE / TOPIC, for use inside a desk.

     Once a reader is plainly inside Technology, repeating TECHNOLOGY
     on every card tells them nothing. The desk drops away and the type
     takes the front of the label. Neither half is emphasised, because
     the coloured half of a label is the desk, and the desk is exactly
     what has been established.

     Both desks are skipped, so a story tagged Technology and then
     Philosophy does not read as though Philosophy were its type.

     There is no wrapper element. foreach cannot stop at the first
     match, so each eligible tag prints its own label and CSS keeps the
     first two; a wrapper would have to be printed before anything was
     known about what goes in it, and a story carrying only a desk tag
     would then leave an empty label in the markup for a screen reader
     to find. Printing nothing is better than hiding something. --}}

{{~#foreach tags from="2"~}}
{{~#match slug "!=" "technology"~}}
{{~#match slug "!=" "philosophy"~}}<span class="lc-label lc-label--desk">{{name}}</span>{{~/match~}}
{{~/match~}}
{{~/foreach~}}
